def ev(p,*rs):
 p='pfp/domain/'+p;return {'path':p,'sha256':a.row(p)['sha256'],'lines':[list(x) for x in rs]}
for number,title,s,es,ids in [
(85,'Prompt audit is a fixture-specific heuristic','Nonsingular x+y=5,2x+4y=10 is refused as singular because one literal equation matches; singular x+2y=5,3x+6y=15 is unflagged. Reversed balanced delimiters >< also pass. Coefficient/substring and delimiter counts are not determinant or grammar checks, despite broad allperturbed prompts fail-closed prose.',[ev('pilots/fail_closed_gate.py',(13,14),(91,151))],[107]),
(86,'Intermediate witness check accepts negated bindings and unknown checker','The text saying x=1 and y=2 are both false passes the binding regex; an unknown checker with nonempty text also gets ACCEPTED. Neither substitution nor semantic truth of intermediates is tested. This may be a lexical extraction control, but its verified wording is too strong.',[ev('pilots/fail_closed_gate.py',(720,759))],[108]),
(87,'Graph oracle comparison conflates boolean and integer fields','The graph-facts gate accepts integer1/0 in boolean fields and True as edge_count1 because nested dictionary equality equates these values. It validates required keys but not their types. Trusted expected-answer equality also remains distinct from independent topology checking.',[ev('pilots/fail_closed_gate.py',(275,305),(344,369))],[109]),
(88,'Determinant sign-flip fixture and diagnostic are arithmetically wrong','For [[3,7],[2,5]], ad-bc=1 and bc-ad=-1, not-11. The fixture calls-11 a sign flip and runtime reserves that diagnosis for-11; actual-1 receives arithmetic-error code. Both are correctly refused against1, so defect concerns explanation and mutation classification, not false acceptance.',[ev('fixtures/negative_mutation_fixtures.yaml',(337,346),(359,368)),ev('pilots/fail_closed_gate.py',(669,687))],[110]),
(89,'Pilot aggregate equality bypasses checker type restrictions','PilotAggregate._answer_matches returnsTrue directly for extracted True and expected1, while the linalg gate refuses boolean candidates. Therefore its ACCEPTED invariant does not preserve the checker representation rules as claimed; Python equality short-circuits the fallback. Probe exercises unchanged comparison method, not full state transitions.',[ev('aggregates/pilot_aggregate.py',(35,38),(102,108),(123,133)),ev('pilots/fail_closed_gate.py',(421,432))],[111])]:n['findings'].append({'id':'PFPDOMAIN-F'+str(number).zfill(3),'title':title,'statement':s,'evidence':[e['path'] for e in es],'source_evidence':es,'control_ids':['PFPDOMAIN-C'+str(i).zfill(3) for i in ids],'status':'confirmed_bounded_source_and_probe','limits':'Synthetic independent examples and read-vetted gate owner. No retained private benchmark, provider or original source execution outside pure domain functions.'})
es=[ev('provenance/three_role_gate.py',(15,18),(292,343)),ev('pilots/fail_closed_gate.py',(429,439),(487,528),(566,595))]
n['claims'].append({'id':'PFPDOMAIN-CL22','title':'Declared role separation and trusted-oracle comparison remain distinct','statement':'ThreeRoleGate checks host scope/admitted-root membership and declared pairwise role/principal separation; it neither authenticates independent actors nor evaluates claims. Pilot gates enforce useful finite integer/list/schema comparisons against supplied oracle data, while oracle adequacy and source binding remain external. Neither role separation nor answer matching establishes PFP as a universal scientific verifier.','evidence':[e['path'] for e in es],'source_evidence':es,'status':'bounded_source_assessment'})
